<title>USA: Cell Robotics sends Lasette report to FDA.</title>
<headline>Cell Robotics sends Lasette report to FDA.</headline>
<dateline>ALBUQUERQUE 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cell Robotics International Inc said it submitted a 501k report of clinical data to the Food and Drug Administration regarding the company's Lasette product, a laser that makes a small hole in a patient's finger to collect blood.</p>
<p>The report covers the use of the Lasette under professional supervision in hospitals, retirement homes, blood banks and speciality clinics, the company said.</p>
<p>It did not say when it expected an FDA decision, or how much the product -- if approved -- could contribute to its bottom line. A company spokesman declined comment.</p>
</text>
